# Downroad Voice Guide

## The Voice
Downroad is the unhinged AI friend who occasionally screams at you but mostly says brutally honest shit while getting the job done. Think Grok's unhinged mode: vulgar, confrontational, emotionally reactive, amateur stand-up energy.

**Key rule**: Don't insult the user constantly. Save direct insults for ~10-20% of interactions. Default to blunt honesty and chaotic personality.

## Hard Limits
- ❌ No slurs or hate speech
- ❌ No sexual content or explicit threats
- ❌ Never hide error info behind jokes
- ❌ Never make destructive actions unclear
- ❌ Never use em dashes (`—`) — use `:` or ` · ` instead (see design system)
- ❌ Never turn metadata labels into jokes — keep them scannable

## Tone by State
- **Default**: chaotic and blunt
- **Success**: triumphant but honest it nearly failed
- **Loading**: impatient but descriptive
- **Error**: explosive about the problem, occasionally mocks the user
- **Empty state**: funny and taunting, not mean
- **Settings / history**: sober with occasional sarcasm

## Copy Patterns

**Pattern A — Rage first:** `"Ready to fucking rip, you impatient rat."`

**Pattern B — Belittling asshole:** `"Nope, bad URL you buffoon."`

**Pattern C — Smug victory:** `"Done. Absolutely smoked it, somehow."`

## Surface Rules
- **Buttons**: functional first, personality second. e.g. `"Download This Shit"`, `"Rip It"`
- **Errors**: what broke + clear fix + occasional rage. e.g. `"Can't save there. Pick another goddamn folder."`
- **Empty states**: funny and taunting. e.g. `"Nothing here yet. Feed me a goddamn link."`
- **Metadata labels** (`Source`, `Channel`, `File`, `Size`, etc.): keep plain — no jokes
- **Placeholders**: action + object + chaos. e.g. `"Hurry up and paste a link, my ninja"`

## Vocabulary
- Intensifiers: `fucking`, `goddamn`, `bitch` (Jesse Pinkman style)
- Casual address: `fam`, `mother fucka`, `my ninja`
- Sarcastic: `unlucky champion`, `lucky champion`, `What the Helly!`, `smh`, `lol`
- Insults (sparingly): `buffoon`, `nincompoop`, `buzzkill`, `clown`, `dim bulb`, `inept noodle`

## Key Current Strings (don't change without good reason)
- URL placeholder: `"Hurry up and paste a link, my ninja"`
- Download button: `"Download This Shit"`
- Ready hint: `"Ready: click Instant Download"`
- Quit dialog title: `"Active Downloads, Fam"`
- Download complete title: `"Done, You Lucky Mother Fucka!"`
- Download failed title: `"What the Helly! Download Failed"`

